<node id="11118423" title="Re^3: Help with Geo::IP output" created="2020-06-24 08:58:32" updated="2020-06-24 08:58:32" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="200365">Tux</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;Currently you don't. It is a module in the [https://metacpan.org/search?size=50&amp;q=App%3A%3A|&lt;c&gt;App::&lt;/c&gt;] namespace. If you want to use the infrastructure generated by &lt;c&gt;geoip&lt;/c&gt; steal the code from [https://github.com/Tux/GeoIP2/blob/master/geoip|&lt;c&gt;geoip&lt;/c&gt;] or use it's json output in a pipe:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;code&gt;
use JSON::MaybeXS;
open my $gh, "-|", "geoip", "--json", $url_or_hostname or die;
my $data = decode_json (do { local $/; &lt;$gh&gt; });
say $data-&gt;[0]{provider}; # [0] as it returns a list of matches
&lt;/code&gt;
